                <pb facs="0279" n="269" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg269"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.48/1449a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Algiers</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wiley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-03-13T21:00:00-04:00">March 13, 1943—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>457. For Murphy. American Embassy Madrid has requested allocation of $100,000 per
                    month of American funds for relief of refugees of French nationality in Spain.
                    This request is predicated on statement from Madrid that although 25,000,000
                    francs have been voted by French North African regime for relief of French
                    refugees in Spain there are no immediate prospects of any substantial portion of
                    peseta proceeds becoming available to Malaise and at present he is not even
                    receiving enough to pay off back indebtedness.</p>
                <p>The following telegram has been dispatched to Madrid in reply:</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of telegram No. 577, March 13, 9 p.m., to the Ambassador in
                    Spain, printed <hi rendition="#italic">supra.</hi>]</p>
                <p>Please indicate to the French that it is difficult for us to assume further
                    financial responsibility at present and that it would be desirable for them to
                    follow the procedure proposed in the telegram to Madrid.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
